Public framegeneration headers from the same revision, under src/fsr/include/framegeneration.
Owned changes remove legacy foreign-private-C++ ABI calls and AntiLag vendor transport. Shared public NGX/FSR generation uses the pinned MIT ordinary-DXIL optical-flow/interpolation backend under backend/, not MetalFX encode success as an outcome. Native MetalFX SR/FG implementation remains separate.

Public DLL ordinals preserve the reference Wine spec: Configure=1, CreateContext=2, DestroyContext=3, Dispatch=4, Query=5.
Only the owned D3D12 renderer is accepted; there is no native-vendor renderer fallback. The public one-output path is now the same genuine SDK algorithm as multi-output, not a MetalFX fast path; its performance and output differ from the previous implementation.
The owned grouped contract accepts one to four distinct single-sample 2D outputs. Every count uses the genuine SDK phase backend; phases are i/(N+1), with one history advance per real pair. Direct public dispatch must explicitly enable frame generation with Configure before Prepare; a context without a proxy is not implicitly enabled by presentation. Generate requires a matching current-epoch Prepare; a newer queued Prepare does not replace that immutable input or imply a reset of the earlier matching generation. Rejected generation does not retire unrelated prepared metadata. Disabling or destroying a context cancels unsubmitted packets; completed generated pixels remain immutable during later closed-list replay. A maximum of 64 unretired configured frame IDs and no reserved generation flags remain explicit limits.
The manual FSR proxy retains two independent four-output banks and consumes only GPU-validated actual counts after the submitted interpolation fence. Bootstrap, reset, scene-change, stale and disabled batches publish no generated frames; no CopyCurrent frame is labeled generated. Generated phases precede the real frame exactly once (or only generated phases in generated-only mode); zero-count generated-only batches retire their reserved fence serials without presenting. No ordinary DXGI swapchain injection is installed.
Tear lines, reset/scene indicators, and debug view use the pinned SDK full-display diagnostics; their overlays can extend outside the normal generation rectangle. These diagnostics are not a substitute for GPU actual-count validation. Debug view selects generated-only presentation as in the MIT provider. Configure and per-frame Prepare flags and recorded generation regions are immutable; independent production-valid GPU baselines check capture across newer Prepare and later Configure/descriptor mutation without fixing a vendor panel layout or palette. Full-output closed-list replay remains exact after context destruction, and debug output never seeds real-pair history. Normal all-count outputs retain exact current-REAL pixels outside the generation rectangle. Prepare and Generate retain normalized shader flags (bits 0..2), combined per recorded phase; provider-only lifecycle/pacing flags are not shader flags, and unknown bits remain rejected.
ResizeBuffers1 retains validated per-buffer presentation queues and forwards them to DXGI; generated, real, and UI output use the current physical buffer queue with ordered fence retirement and drain-before-resize atomic rollback. The public callback consumer's blocked-queue oracle follows accepted outputs from drained prior batches around the physical ring, not a hardcoded REAL-frame schedule, requested interpolation count, or OS displayed count; pending GPU markers, idle-queue progress, and unchanged native presentation statistics remain required until release.
Swapchain memory queries retain the MIT provider accounting.
Callback and native Present failures suppress unwritten/rejected output while still retiring the existing presentation fence graph; asynchronous failures are observable through the public wait-for-presents dispatch. Explicit result retention is requested only for dispatches captured by an active or registered proxy command list, not merely because a context has an attached proxy or a NO_SWAPCHAIN_CONTEXT_NOTIFY flag. Direct dispatch relinquishes metadata after validated GPU completion without requiring an unavailable public outcome query; the proxy releases retained outcomes after result observation and composition GPU retirement.

Backend source is the 75-file compiler dependency closure of the pinned revision, not the full SDK. backend/produce-shaders.py reproduces 39 generic FP32 cs_6_2 kernels with official DXC 1.9.2609.5; backend/shaders/provenance.json records compiler and bytecode SHA-256. No forced wave64 or FP16 fallback is used. The retained-geometry MIT extension transports previous real depth/motion and uses asymmetric phase endpoint sampling; scene/reset/bootstrap produce GPU actual count zero and leave generated outputs untouched. Prepare depth/MV and Generate color/HUDless are captured once per REAL packet. Per-packet immutable descriptor/constant arenas prevent queued CPU recording from overwriting pending GPU arguments. Arena capacity is derived once per state from actual reflected table spans and the bounded one-REAL graph: one Prepare, 24 optical-flow dispatches, reverse/splat plus ceil(log2(maxRenderDimension)) jump-flood dispatches once, and at most 12 interpolation/debug dispatches per phase. Each reflected constant buffer uses one compile-time-bounded 256-byte slot. Immutable packets omit the persistent SDK ring/static descriptor region, never wrap, and return allocation failure on exhaustion; their ownership still extends through retained command-list/publication references. Initialized DEFAULT resources finish their queued upload with an explicit transition from transient COPY_DEST to the declared initial state; trailing SDK barriers flush before execution returns, so bootstrap initializes static inputs without leaving their CPU state cache stale for later immutable packets. Only the final phase commits current REAL history; UI never seeds interpolation history. Publication uses the retained actual-count buffer to select one-based NGX outputs and write OutputDisableInterpolation without copying undefined output. Generated color writes explicit opaque RGBA independently of the inpainting mask; current-REAL movie bars outside the interpolation rectangle retain the SDK policy. Jittered motion uses the real previous-minus-current render-pixel jitter delta normalized to UV, captured once in Prepare and retained across all phases. Private input/color snapshots remain COPY_DEST at each recorded stage boundary; generation transitions them to shader-read only for SDK consumption and restores COPY_DEST after final REAL history/count copies, so no-copy closed-list replay remains state-valid.
